WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.520
This is The Spread, your energy
markets briefing for Monday,

2
00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:08.080
the ninth of November. This episode
is written and read with AI.

3
00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:12.160
Iraq says Washington has agreed a
lane for its oil exports through the

4
00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.320
Strait of Hormuz, near Oman.

5
00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:16.400
Only Baghdad has said so.

6
00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:20.960
Meanwhile, US forces disabled a ship
trying to run the Iran blockade,

7
00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:25.200
after a week in which crude prices
fell hard on bets that peace is coming

8
00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:26.960
faster than the fighting suggests.

9
00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:32.000
On the markets. Brent ended last week
around ninety-nine dollars a barrel,

10
00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:35.760
down about fifteen percent,
according to OilPrice dot com.

11
00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:40.000
Rigzone reports that was the
biggest weekly drop since 2022.

12
00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:43.760
December West Texas Intermediate
lost eleven dollars forty on the week

13
00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:46.560
and touched eighty-six dollars seventy.

14
00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:50.640
EU gas storage was seventy-two point
seven percent full on Saturday,

15
00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:54.240
according to Gas Infrastructure
Europe, down from seventy-three point

16
00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:56.000
eight on Wednesday.

17
00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:00.160
Iraq's foreign minister, Fuad Hussein,
said on Sunday that Baghdad has

18
00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:02.920
reached understandings
with the United States.

19
00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:06.920
Those would let Iraqi crude transit
Hormuz through a lane near Oman,

20
00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:10.600
Reuters reported. There is no
US statement in the reports,

21
00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:13.640
and neither the route nor
any volume has been given.

22
00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:17.760
If it holds, Iraq's medium-sour
barrels would move on a US-sanctioned

23
00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:20.827
route rather than
through one-off transits.

24
00:01:20.853 --> 00:01:23.640
The claim comes as Gulf supply recovers.

25
00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:27.893
A Bloomberg survey puts October
OPEC output close to pre-war levels,

26
00:01:27.947 --> 00:01:32.160
led by Saudi Arabia. Iraq's oil
minister says the country already pumps

27
00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:34.520
more than five million barrels a day.

28
00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:37.800
That is over half a million
above its OPEC plus requirement,

29
00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:41.520
which is awkward six days after
Baghdad agreed to hold December targets

30
00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:42.920
unchanged.

31
00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:46.280
For some buyers, ships are
now the binding constraint.

32
00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:49.920
The chairman of Hindustan Petroleum
told Bloomberg the Indian refiner

33
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.680
is struggling to hire
tankers for Gulf loadings,

34
00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:55.787
even with crude flows near pre-war levels.

35
00:01:55.813 --> 00:01:59.200
Staying in the region, the blockade
of Iran turned kinetic again over

36
00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:03.920
the weekend. On Saturday a US military
aircraft fired on and disabled

37
00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:07.720
a commercial vessel trying to break
the blockade in the Gulf of Oman,

38
00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:10.040
according to US Central Command.

39
00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:13.080
That evening, explosions
hit southern Iran.

40
00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:17.040
Iranian media framed them as Iran's
own military activity rather than

41
00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:20.760
US strikes, and both
sides reported ships hit.

42
00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:22.480
Crews are paying the price.

43
00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:26.320
A seafarer was killed on Thursday
in a suspected missile strike on the

44
00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:30.240
Velos Sapphire, a Greek-managed
product tanker of about seventy-five

45
00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:33.600
thousand deadweight
tonnes, inside the Gulf.

46
00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:36.640
Iran has also reshuffled
its Hormuz blacklist,

47
00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:38.960
Splash twenty-four seven reported.

48
00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:44.080
The consultancy FGE NexantECA says
Iranian exports are near zero under

49
00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:48.480
the blockade. It sees slim odds of
a deal and calls the next two months

50
00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:51.360
the period of highest escalation risk.

51
00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:54.800
Back to last week's sell-off,
where the trigger was political.

52
00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:57.200
Republicans lost both
chambers of Congress,

53
00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:01.600
and Vice President Vance blamed the
war, according to OilPrice dot com.

54
00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:04.160
That fed bets on de-escalation.

55
00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.560
The banks' balances point the same way.

56
00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:10.400
JPMorgan estimates the market ran
a surplus of one point one million

57
00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:12.613
barrels a day in September.

58
00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:16.640
It sees that widening to one point
four million in October as high prices

59
00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:20.040
cut demand. Product markets moved first.

60
00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:23.840
Asia's high-sulphur fuel oil margin
slipped to a discount of two dollars

61
00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:28.080
thirty a barrel on Thursday,
as more Gulf oil reaches Asia.

62
00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:32.040
Over in Russia, Ukraine has now hit
a sixth Russian refinery within a

63
00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:36.240
week, Rigzone reported. Three were
hit between the thirtieth of October

64
00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:38.107
and the second of November.

65
00:03:38.133 --> 00:03:40.800
The latest are new strikes, not a recount,

66
00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:43.800
though damage and idled
capacity aren't reported.

67
00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:46.240
Moscow's budget shows the strain.

68
00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:50.080
Subsidies paid to producers to keep
road fuels at home are at their highest

69
00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:54.840
in more than four years. The diesel
export ban has already been extended,

70
00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:58.960
so every lost run means less
Russian product for buyers abroad.

71
00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:02.960
Separately, Russia says overnight
strikes hit three cargo ships carrying

72
00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:06.400
military goods for Ukraine,
plus two substations.

73
00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:10.240
That is Moscow's claim alone, with
no ship names and no response from

74
00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:11.240
Kyiv.

75
00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:15.840
On shipping, Trafigura, Vitol,
Mercuria and the Abu Dhabi National Oil

76
00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:19.800
Company, or ADNOC, are
negotiating with US officials.

77
00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:23.733
They want licences to buy or lease
about fifty sanctioned tankers,

78
00:04:23.787 --> 00:04:27.160
and Treasury is weighing
approvals, according to Bloomberg.

79
00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:31.600
The report rests on unnamed sources,
and Treasury hasn't commented.

80
00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:34.560
Freight is already
reshaping crude pricing.

81
00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:37.920
Soaring tanker rates have pushed
sellers to deepen discounts on heavy

82
00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:42.080
grades, Reuters reported, which
gives US Gulf Coast refiners cheaper

83
00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:47.120
feedstock. According to the EIA, US
imports of Venezuelan crude averaged

84
00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:50.040
seven hundred and one thousand
barrels a day in July,

85
00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:55.040
the most since May 2017. They eased
to six hundred and fifty-five thousand

86
00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:59.520
in August. More tonnage, if licensed,
could narrow those discounts.

87
00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.000
A few more things.

88
00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:05.280
Energy Aspects now expects China to
export about five hundred and eighty

89
00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:08.960
thousand tonnes of diesel in
November, Bloomberg reported.

90
00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:11.920
That's four hundred thousand
below its earlier estimate,

91
00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:15.920
because Chinese inventories have fallen,
which leaves Asia's diesel market

92
00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:20.720
tighter. The figure could be revised
up if domestic demand weakens.

93
00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:24.600
Egypt has told fertiliser producers
their gas supply will be cut by a

94
00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:28.320
further thirty-three percent,
according to a company statement.

95
00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:32.560
In Norway, the regulator Havtil is
investigating a fire in the switchboard

96
00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:35.680
room on the Equinor-operated Visund field.

97
00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:40.080
Adani Ports is buying the Dutch storage
operator Evos for about two point

98
00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:41.920
six billion euros.

99
00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:46.400
ADNOC has signed a ten-year liquefied
natural gas deal with Gujarat Energy,

100
00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:50.160
starting in 2028. It's the
company's fifth in India,

101
00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:52.840
and reported volumes
differ between sources.

102
00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:56.000
And the US rig count rose
to six hundred and four,

103
00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:57.480
according to Baker Hughes.

104
00:05:57.680 --> 00:06:01.200
Oil rigs were up one, to
four hundred and sixty-three.

105
00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:05.600
What to watch next. Daily EU storage
readings from Gas Infrastructure

106
00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:07.600
Europe through the nineteenth of November.

107
00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:11.920
Then on Wednesday, the EIA weekly
report for the week to the sixth of

108
00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:14.680
November, with distillate stocks in focus.

109
00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:20.000
Further out: Guyana's first Uaru
cargo, the EU ban on long-term Russian

110
00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:24.240
liquefied natural gas imports, and
the expiry of Russia's diesel export

111
00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:27.760
ban, all between mid-December
and the end of January.

112
00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:31.520
That's the brief. Sources for everything
you heard are in the show notes.
